{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# DocTamper Data Preparation & Preprocessing Pipeline - Phase 1\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the execution of the Phase 1 pipeline, covering: \n",
    "- Centralized configuration via `config.yaml`\n",
    "- Pre-pipeline integrity validation\n",
    "- Unified sample parsing\n",
    "- Multi-region bounding box generation from masks\n",
    "- Data augmentations with spatial synchronization\n",
    "- Hugging Face Qwen2-VL compatibility structures\n",
    "- Reusable PyTorch dataloaders for train, val, and test splits\n",
    "- Statistics generation (JSON and CSV)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports and Environment Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure project root is in system path\n",
    "project_root = Path(\"\").resolve().parent\n",
    "if str(project_root) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.append(str(project_root))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.config import DatasetConfig\n",
    "from src.validation import run_prepipeline_validation\n",
    "from src.dataset import DocTamperTorchDataset\n",
    "from src.dataset_loader import get_dataloaders\n",
    "from src.statistics import generate_split_statistics_report\n",
    "from src.visualization import visualize_preprocessed_sample\n",
    "from src.processor import Qwen2VLDataProcessor\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Environment initialized successfully!\")\n",
    "print(\"CUDA Available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load Configuration Settings\n",
    "\n",
    "We load all processing, dataloader, model prompts, and output directories directly from `config.yaml`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "config = DatasetConfig()\n",
    "print(\"Active configuration root paths:\")\n",
    "print(config)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAugmentations enabled: {config.aug_enabled}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target image resolution: {config.image_size}\")\n",
    "print(f\"DataLoader batch size: {config.batch_size}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Pre-Pipeline Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "Verify that the necessary subsets exist and check a quick sample slice (e.g. 50 samples) for image/mask readability, matching dimensions, and correct binarity before starting the pipeline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "validation_ready = run_prepipeline_validation(config, sample_limit=50)\n",
    "print(f\"Pipeline Readiness Status: {'READY' if validation_ready else 'NOT READY'}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Single Sample Inspection & Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's load the PyTorch-compatible `DocTamperTorchDataset` and inspect the unified dictionary format for a single sample. This also applies data augmentations (fallback or Albumentations) and extracts bounding boxes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the dataset wrapper for the Training Set (without augmentations for inspection)\n",
    "dataset = DocTamperTorchDataset(config.training_set, config=config, augment=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "with dataset:\n",
    "    # Get unified representation dict for sample index 0\n",
    "    sample = dataset[0]\n",
    "    \n",
    "print(\"Unified Sample Dictionary keys:\", list(sample.keys()))\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSample ID: {sample['sample_id']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Image size (original): {sample['width']}x{sample['height']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Image size (preprocessed): {sample['image'].size}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Tampering Label: {sample['tampering_label']} (1=Tampered, 0=Authentic)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Forgery Type: {sample['forgery_type']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Prompt: '{sample['prompt']}'\")\n",
    "print(f\"Extracted Bounding Boxes count: {len(sample['bbox'])}\")\n",
    "if len(sample['bbox']) > 0:\n",
    "    print(f\"First Bounding Box (absolute): {sample['bbox'][0]}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"First Bounding Box (normalized Qwen2-VL scale 1000): {sample['normalized_bbox'][0]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Inline Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "We visualize the preprocessed document image, the binary mask, and the overlay blend with drawn bounding boxes, forgery labels, and VLM prompts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Render the preprocessed sample inline\n",
    "visualize_preprocessed_sample(sample, alpha=0.5, show=True);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. DataLoader Creation & Split Statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's split a small slice of 200 samples into Train (80%), Val (10%), and Test (10%), build the corresponding PyTorch dataloaders, and compile the final split statistics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_loader, val_loader, test_loader = get_dataloaders(\n",
    "    config.training_set, \n",
    "    config=config, \n",
    "    sample_limit=200\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate splits report\n",
    "stats_report = generate_split_statistics_report(\n",
    "    train_loader.dataset,\n",
    "    val_loader.dataset,\n",
    "    test_loader.dataset,\n",
    "    config.statistics_dir\n")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Hugging Face Qwen2-VL Processor Integration\n",
    "\n",
    "We demonstrate formatting VLM prompts, converting images, and loading Hugging Face compatible tokens using our Qwen2VLDataProcessor (relying on its robust fallback if running in offline mode)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "processor = Qwen2VLDataProcessor(processor_name=config.processor_name)\n",
    "vlm_inputs = processor.process_sample(sample)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Processor Tensors:\", list(vlm_inputs.keys()))\n",
    "print(\"Input IDs tensor shape:\", vlm_inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape)\n",
    "print(\"Pixel values tensor shape:\", vlm_inputs[\"pixel_values\"].shape)\n",
    "print(\"Is fallback active (offline):\", vlm_inputs.get(\"is_fallback\", False))"
   ]
  }
 ],
